NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0179e5946e962f23a27f788023b036187ddd500962a68bbfb2eb8679952db29a","event_uuid":"51f1b07a-691a-4b24-8751-aced9a2b8b88","position":{"commit_sha":"a37d4c2bb006af839495ef0be4891e7dcf9d34a2","position":"1785726589704509001-51f1b07a-691a-4b24-8751-aced9a2b8b88"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete, pushed as Gerrit change 1265 (commit 025cf1c3bb, stacked on 1262/1257).\n\nTest-only change (authored directly per plan; no implementer subagent needed):\n- tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py — hoisted _git/_rebar_cli(+timeout)/_clear_sync_throttle/build_repo_with_origin_tickets from test_show_no_stall.py\n- tests/interfaces/store/conftest.py — shared repo_with_origin_tickets fixture (REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off during build, REBAR_ROOT pinned)\n- tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py — refactored to import the harness; both ed2b tests byte-for-byte identical in behavior (2 passed post-refactor)\n- tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py — the generalized property, table-driven over show/list/search/ready: (A) write-burst storm — 3 rounds of edit bursts with background pushes, per-surface throttle clear, exit0 => stdout parses as documented JSON shape (dict for show, list for list/search/ready; valid-empty [] passes, truncated-empty fails); (B) deterministic held-write-lock — thread holds lock.acquire(timeout=30), each surface must complete within 10s.\n\nProbed before writing: search with zero matches emits [] exit 0 (not empty text), ready --output json emits JSON array — so the shape assertions hold vacuously-safely on empty stores.\n\nRED demonstrated: reverting _RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT 2 -> 15 (the writer default that caused ed2b) fails test B (show stalls >10s). Restored, all green: 4 passed in module+refactored pair; full tier 323 passed (1 pre-existing env-specific failure in test_tracker_config_e2e — git for-each-ref exit 128 on temp bare remote, fails identically on clean stash tree, unrelated).","timestamp":1785726589704509001}],"created_at":1785640220988324001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"708f41cc-e3df-4dbc-99c0-1647c76c820e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"74e1-36fd-e445-49a2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\ned2b (`rebar show` intermittently returned EMPTY stdout with exit 0 under concurrent background auto-push) was fixed by bounding the read-path reconverge lock wait (`_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT = 2` in `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`) and landed with a show-only regression test (`tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py`). But read-output integrity under sync contention is a GENERIC property of every read surface that routes through `ensure_fresh` — list, search, ready, next-batch share the same reconverge path as show and would regress silently (bug-trend review change 20: one-time machinery, no bespoke per-surface copies).\n\n## Approach\nGeneralize the existing ed2b harness rather than inventing a new storm: reuse/hoist `repo_with_origin_tickets` + the `_rebar_cli` helper from `test_show_no_stall.py` into a sibling property module. One property-style test parameterized over the CLI read surfaces (`show`, `list`, `search`, `ready` at minimum): under the same burst-of-writes contention (each `rebar edit` spawning a background push via `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`), every ZERO-exit read invocation must produce PARSEABLE output for its format. Use each surface's JSON spelling — `--output json` where the flag exists (show/list/ready); `search` takes no output flag and already emits a JSON array by default — and pin: exit 0 implies stdout parses as JSON of the surface's documented shape (list/object). This sidesteps legitimately-empty text output — e.g. `rebar ready` in default text mode prints nothing when no tickets are unblocked — because valid-empty serializes as `[]`, distinguishable from truncated-empty stdout. A LOUD nonzero exit is acceptable — empty-success is the bug. Explicitly NOT pagination invariants: rebar's read CLI has no cursor/offset pagination; the property is output-integrity-or-loud-error.\n\nThrottle handling (decisive): `ensure_fresh` reconverges at most 1/min per store via the `/tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5(tracker)>` marker, so only the first read in a window can stall. The harness must call the existing `_clear_sync_throttle(tracker)` helper (already in `test_show_no_stall.py:69`) BEFORE EACH parameterized read invocation so every surface actually exercises the reconverge path rather than short-circuiting to the local snapshot.\n\n## Scope\n- tests/interfaces/store/ — new sibling module + minimal fixture/helper hoist (no production code)\n\n## Testing\nThe test IS the deliverable. RED demonstration: temporarily revert the ed2b ledge locally (raise `_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT` back to the 15s writer default so reads stall on the held lock) and observe the property fail on at least one surface; restore and confirm green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One parameterized property covers show/list/search/ready via the real CLI under the ed2b write-burst + background-push harness; no bespoke per-surface copies.\n- [ ] Invariant pinned: exit 0 implies stdout parses as the surface's JSON shape (valid-empty `[]` passes; truncated/empty stdout fails); nonzero exits pass (loud failure allowed).\n- [ ] Throttle marker cleared before each read so every invocation exercises the reconverge path.\n- [ ] RED demonstrated by locally reverting the reads.py lock-timeout ledge; green on the fixed tree.\n- [ ] ed2b harness reused (hoisted or imported), not duplicated.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py","reason":"read-under-storm property"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","74e1-36fd-e445-49a2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"9f7f9071-4070-44c8-9163-9a55ca96d7b0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["concurrency","tests"],"ticket_id":"fa6e-78c8-f806-4283","ticket_type":"task","title":"Concurrency suite: generic reads-under-writer-storm property","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2a556638-d130-4b65-a7e7-d41c3b97f1e0","3a103efc-7871-4428-a4c2-f0654c2e1493","e7a68ab1-0045-4a01-b49b-e3c4f0080964","36781839-a443-4b5c-9b4d-0734e85bec73","c9205e4f-e28a-422e-9bcc-c56566ebb9c3","1d75af4a-a2d5-410b-b2c4-c0bf4982803d","9f7f9071-4070-44c8-9163-9a55ca96d7b0","da583b27-adb2-4584-a293-150478a33212","51f1b07a-691a-4b24-8751-aced9a2b8b88","708f41cc-e3df-4dbc-99c0-1647c76c820e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785728358774145950,"uuid":"8f676923-9364-486c-8891-190f3f308fb9"}